1. UNAUTHENTICATED
The user has not logged in yet.

No access to any feature

Shows login page

Awaiting email, password, and optional OTP

2. AUTHENTICATED_PENDING_VERIFICATION
User has logged in, but domain/org check is pending.

System checks if the user is from an approved agency (e.g., @gov.in)

Shows a verification loading screen or confirmation

3. AUTHORIZED
User is verified and successfully logged in.

System assigns a role (Admin, Analyst, Observer)

User is taken to the dashboard

4. FILE_UPLOADED
The user has uploaded a locked/encrypted file.

File metadata is extracted

File type detection begins

File is stored temporarily or encrypted

5. FILE_TYPE_DETECTED
System confirms what kind of file was uploaded.

Examples: ZIP, PDF, DOCX, XLSX, RAR

Used to pick the right cracking tool

6. CRACKING_IN_PROGRESS
The system is actively trying to unlock the file.

Dictionary attack or brute force begins

AI predictions (if enabled) are being used

Progress bar or log updates shown to user

7. PASSWORD_FOUND
The correct password has been discovered.

Password is stored securely

File is decrypted for viewing

System moves to viewing phase

8. PASSWORD_NOT_FOUND
The cracking failed (e.g., exhausted all possibilities).

Shows failure message

Logs the attempt for reporting

Offers retry with different dictionary or AI settings

9. FILE_DECRYPTED
File has been successfully opened.

Decrypted file is rendered in secure viewer

Viewer is limited by role (read-only for Analyst, export only for Admin)

Logs viewer access

10. REPORT_GENERATED
System creates a full report of what happened.

Includes time taken, user role, methods used, outcome

PDF report saved to logs or sent to admin

11. SESSION_EXPIRED
User is inactive or timeout occurred.

Files auto-deleted

User must re-login or re-upload

Used for legal compliance and security

12. MISUSE_DETECTED
Suspicious activity triggered a security block.

Multiple failed attempts

Repeated exports or login failures

User is auto-blocked, and admin is notified
